  {
    "path": "packages/browser-devtools/README.md",
    "sha256": "76a62792a7713734235a9f51e4f934023b6c42c354c06d9ecb3cb5e3f1e31096",
    "captureTiming": "After actual source displays60bcce/57917f/1e4ccc/9911ff/ac6f5d, only previously displayed lines; same navigation regexes reproduce those original displayed matches. Not first-read/pre-read snapshot.",
    "displayedLines": [
      {
        "line": 1,
        "text": "# Browser DevTools diagnostics"
      },
      {
        "line": 2,
        "text": ""
      },
      {
        "line": 3,
        "text": "`@cjhyy/code-shell-browser-devtools` is a private, zero-runtime-dependency module"
      },
      {
        "line": 4,
        "text": "for bounded browser diagnostics. It accepts an injected page surface compatible"
      },
      {
        "line": 5,
        "text": "with Puppeteer and Playwright. It does not import either library, Electron, or"
      },
      {
        "line": 6,
        "text": "CodeShell Core."
      },
      {
        "line": 7,
        "text": ""
      },
      {
        "line": 8,
        "text": "```ts"
      },
      {
        "line": 9,
        "text": "import { createBrowserInspector } from \"@cjhyy/code-shell-browser-devtools\";"
      },
      {
        "line": 10,
        "text": ""
      },
      {
        "line": 11,
        "text": "// The host resolves and authorizes this exact page before passing it here."
      },
      {
        "line": 12,
        "text": "const inspector = createBrowserInspector(page);"
      },
      {
        "line": 13,
        "text": ""
      },
      {
        "line": 14,
        "text": "await inspector.inspect({ mode: \"network\" });"
      },
      {
        "line": 15,
        "text": "// Reproduce the issue on the same document, then read recent records."
      },
      {
        "line": 16,
        "text": "const network = await inspector.inspect({ mode: \"network\", maxEntries: 25 });"
      },
      {
        "line": 17,
        "text": "const dom = await inspector.inspect({ mode: \"dom\", selector: \"main\" });"
      },
      {
        "line": 18,
        "text": ""
      },
      {
        "line": 19,
        "text": "// Stop and clear recordings, or dispose when releasing the page."
      },
      {
        "line": 20,
        "text": "await inspector.inspect({ mode: \"stop\" });"
      },
      {
        "line": 21,
        "text": "inspector.dispose();"
      },
      {
        "line": 22,
        "text": "```"
      },
      {
        "line": 23,
        "text": ""
      },
      {
        "line": 24,
        "text": "The exported `BrowserInspectorPage` contract contains only URL/closed-state"
      },
      {
        "line": 25,
        "text": "queries, optional main-frame identity, page evaluation, and event subscription."
      },
      {
        "line": 26,
        "text": "The host owns target selection, browser transport, task grants, domain policy,"
      },
      {
        "line": 27,
        "text": "tool permissions, manual takeover, and any visible Console/Network UI. Inspecting"
      },
      {
        "line": 28,
        "text": "a page does not authorize access to it. The host must dispose the inspector when"
      },
      {
        "line": 29,
        "text": "control is revoked."
      },
      {
        "line": 30,
        "text": ""
      },
      {
        "line": 31,
        "text": "Supported modes preserve the existing Desktop inspector behavior:"
      },
      {
        "line": 32,
        "text": ""
      },
      {
        "line": 33,
        "text": "- `console`: starts recording console messages and page errors on first use;"
      },
      {
        "line": 34,
        "text": "  subsequent calls return recent records."
      },
      {
        "line": 35,
        "text": "- `network`: starts recording response and failed-request metadata. It omits"
      },
      {
        "line": 36,
        "text": "  headers and bodies and strips query strings/fragments from valid HTTP(S) URLs."
      },
      {
        "line": 37,
        "text": "- `dom`: returns a bounded subtree summary of tags, direct text, geometry, and"
      },
      {
        "line": 38,
        "text": "  selected styles. It skips input/editable content and script/style nodes, and"
      },
      {
        "line": 39,
        "text": "  traverses open shadow roots."
      },
      {
        "line": 40,
        "text": "- `performance`: returns bounded navigation, paint, and resource timing summaries."
      },
      {
        "line": 41,
        "text": "- `stop`: removes recording listeners and clears console/network history."
      },
      {
        "line": 42,
        "text": ""
      },
      {
        "line": 43,
        "text": "Each recorder retains at most 100 entries; reads default to 50 and clamp requested"
      },
      {
        "line": 44,
        "text": "limits to 1–100. DOM traversal and page-evaluation waits are bounded. Main-document"
      },
      {
        "line": 45,
        "text": "navigation stops and clears recordings; start recording again on the new"
      },
      {
        "line": 46,
        "text": "document. When the page port omits `mainFrame`, every frame-navigation event"
      },
      {
        "line": 47,
        "text": "clears recordings. Page closure disposes the inspector, and disposal is safe to"
      },
      {
        "line": 48,
        "text": "repeat."
      },
      {
        "line": 49,
        "text": ""
      },
      {
        "line": 50,
        "text": "This is a diagnostics summary API, not a complete DevTools frontend. It has no"
      },
      {
        "line": 51,
        "text": "JavaScript console execution API, debugger/breakpoints, request/response bodies,"
      },
      {
        "line": 52,
        "text": "HAR export, network interception, browser launcher, or cross-frame DOM selector"
      },
      {
        "line": 53,
        "text": "API. Console messages and visible DOM text can still contain sensitive or"
      },
      {
        "line": 54,
        "text": "untrusted page content; consumers remain responsible for handling that output."
      },
      {
        "line": 55,
        "text": "Extracting this module does not change whether native DevTools and browser"
      },
      {
        "line": 56,
        "text": "automation can share a host's debugging connection."
      }
    ]
  }
]
